The problem I see, as mentionned elsewhere, is that there is
that using this method, there is a decided chance of ending up
with teleportitis without teleport control.  If we take your
average case, there is a 60% chance of TC, and an even better
chance of teleportitis.  If you get both, fine (and that's the
most likely result, although probably only around 50%).  If you
get just TC, that's no real problem either, since there will be
plenty of occasions to pick up teleportitis later.  But if you
get just teleportitis... that's a result I wouldn't like at all,
and off hand, without having done the math, I'd guess the
chances of that somewhere between 20-25%.

